>I tried this later with different monsters in different shops.  It
>seems that whenever you attack the shopkeeper with your bare hands,
>and hit him, he doesn't get angry.  If you miss him, he does get 
>angry.  If you use a weapon, he does get angry.  This only works if
>you polymorph into something else, not if you are human and hit him
>with your bare hands.
> 
>I haven't look at the source yet to see why this happens.  Any ideas?
>-- 

I believe that the shopkeeper will react only if attacked by weapon or fist,
and magic attacks.  This leaves attacks such as Claw, Bite, and others
'invisible' to the shopkeeper.  So polying into a monster with these attacks
will allow you to attack the shopkeeper.  This is also probably a bug and
will be fixed in 3.1 (since all missed attacked are noticed)..


